0011: rows for single-channel 16-bit and packed 10-bit in the UBWC compat table.

**Status:** shipped in `27.0.0-devel-p14`. Upstream: not sent - the compat table
row is a candidate, but the argument rests on a measured ceiling on this chip,
which is what an upstream reviewer would want reproduced.
**Found:** probe CEIL: the stock table has no R16 and no packed
10-bit row, so any vkd3d list containing them (R16_TYPELESS and three more
classes) silently lost UBWC.

## For users of other drivers

Nothing to set. R16 and R10G10B10A2 textures in a mutable list keep compression
instead of losing it.

## Summary

`fd6_ubwc_compat_mode()` answers `UNKNOWN` for those formats, and
`tu6_mutable_format_list_ubwc_compatible()` exits on the first unknown member, so
the whole list loses UBWC. That is over-caution, not a hardware limit: a lone
`R16_UNORM` without a list gets a metadata plane on its own. Both formats are
ordinary texture-path citizens with swap `WZYX`
(`fd6_format_table.c:72`, `:209`), and the layout depends only on the block size.

## Evidence

Two hunks in `freedreno_ubwc.h` (enum rows, switch cases). Probe CEIL creates
linear / no-list / mutable images of the same list: `R16_UNORM` no-list `memreq`
`0x82000` against linear `0x80000`, `R10G10B10A2_UNORM` `0x102000` against
`0x100000` - the ceiling exists and the gate is what removes it
(`results/test-CEIL-base.log`, `results/test-CEIL-exp0011.log`, journal 21.6.2).
Isolated A/B on the stack: 3 lines of probe output move
(`results/test-stack.log` vs `results/test-0011.log`).

## Tests

| what the hunk changes | how it is checked | result |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| the two formats keep UBWC in a list | probe CEIL, journal 21.6.2 | metadata plane appears, classes 36 -> 44 |
| isolated effect | the A/B above | 3 lines of probe output, nothing else |
| nothing else moves | the 94-row matrix, journal 24.3 | 94 EXACT |

## The change in this repo

Only `R10G10B10A2_UNORM/_UINT` are added: they are the ones with tiled entries in
`fd6_format_table.c`; SNORM/SINT/USCALED have no tiling there. R8 is deliberately
absent (no ceiling; `has_8bpp_ubwc` stays false, ADR-0007), and so is R32G32B32
(no ceiling measured). The cases hold pipe names, not Vulkan names
(`vk_format.c:114`). Revert: `git apply -R` with the file name explicit.

## Related

`0006`, `0012` (same switch); `0014` (the no-list question).

